---
import ServiceLayout from '../../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
import FAQSchema from '../../components/FAQSchema.astro';
import { serviceFAQs } from '../../data/serviceFAQs';
import { getService } from '../../data/services';

const service = getService('half-head-highlights');

const pageTitle = "Half Head Highlights (1/2 Head Foils) $200";
const pageDescription = "Half head highlights for $200 in Kaukapakapa: foils through the top and sides where colour shows most, with softer regrowth. 2 to 2.5 hours. Book online.";

const faqs = serviceFAQs['half-head-highlights'];
---

<ServiceLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  price={service.price}
  duration={service.duration}
  h1={service.h1}
  serviceName={service.name}
  image="/images/blog/half-head-vs-full-head-foils-1200.webp"
  imageSrcset="/images/blog/half-head-vs-full-head-foils-640.webp 640w, /images/blog/half-head-vs-full-head-foils-1200.webp 1200w, /images/blog/half-head-vs-full-head-foils-1600.webp 1600w"
  imageSizes="100vw"
  imageWidth={1600}
  imageHeight={893}
  imageAlt="Illustration: a hairdresser placing neat rows of foils through the top of a client's hair"
  ogImage="https://hairbymelissa.co.nz/images/blog/half-head-vs-full-head-foils-og.jpg"
>
  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">What is a half head of highlights?</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    A half head of highlights, also called half head foils, places foils through the top, crown and sides of your hair, which is about 50 to 60% of it. The underneath stays natural, so regrowth is softer. At Hair By Melissa it's $200 and takes 2 to 2.5 hours. Comparing options? Read <a href="/blog/half-head-vs-full-head-foils/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">half head vs full head foils</a>. Colouring for an event? See <a href="/blog/christmas-wedding-ball-hair/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">when to book</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Natural Sun-Kissed Dimension Throughout</h2>
  
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    Half head highlights offer the perfect balance between subtle enhancement and noticeable transformation. This service covers the top and sides of your hair, creating beautiful dimension and movement while maintaining a natural look. It's the ideal choice for those wanting significant brightening without the commitment of full head coverage.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Understanding Half Head Highlights</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    Half head highlighting involves applying foils to approximately 50-60% of your hair, focusing on the areas most visible when your hair is styled. This includes the top sections, crown, and sides, leaving the underneath layers in your natural colour. The result is a beautifully blended, multi-dimensional look that appears as if you've spent the summer in the sun.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Why Choose Half Head Highlights?</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 mb-6 space-y-2">
    <li>Creates significant lightness without over-processing</li>
    <li>More natural grow-out than full highlights</li>
    <li>Perfect balance of coverage and maintenance</li>
    <li>Adds depth and dimension throughout visible areas</li>
    <li>Cost-effective compared to full head application</li>
    <li>Suitable for all hair lengths and textures</li>
    <li>Can achieve both subtle and dramatic results</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Perfect For</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
    <div class="bg-[#F8F9FA] rounded-lg p-4">
      <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">First-Time Highlighters</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Great introduction to highlights with manageable maintenance</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-[#F8F9FA] rounded-lg p-4">
      <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Natural Brunettes</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Add warmth and dimension without going too light</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-[#F8F9FA] rounded-lg p-4">
      <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Busy Lifestyles</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Lower maintenance than full highlights</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-[#F8F9FA] rounded-lg p-4">
      <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Budget-Conscious</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Significant impact at a moderate price point</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">The Highlighting Process</h2>
  <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-gray-700 mb-6 space-y-2">
    <li>Detailed consultation to determine desired outcome</li>
    <li>Strategic sectioning for optimal placement</li>
    <li>Custom colour mixing based on your goals</li>
    <li>Precise foil application to selected sections</li>
    <li>Controlled processing with regular checks</li>
    <li>Gentle removal and conditioning treatment</li>
    <li>Toner application for perfect shade</li>
    <li>Professional blow-dry and style</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Colour Options & Techniques</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    Melissa specialises in creating custom highlight shades that complement your natural colour:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 mb-6 space-y-2">
    <li><strong>Babylights:</strong> Ultra-fine highlights for subtle brightness</li>
    <li><strong>Traditional foils:</strong> Classic technique for defined dimension</li>
    <li><strong>Face-framing:</strong> Concentrated brightness around your face</li>
    <li><strong>Ribbon highlights:</strong> Wider sections for bold contrast</li>
    <li><strong>Multi-tonal:</strong> Multiple shades for complex dimension</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Maintenance & Care</h2>
  <div class="bg-[#FFDEE2] bg-opacity-20 rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
    <h3 class="font-semibold mb-3">Extend Your Highlight Life:</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 space-y-2">
      <li>Refresh every 6-8 weeks for optimal appearance</li>
      <li>Use professional colour-protecting products</li>
      <li>Weekly purple shampoo to maintain cool tones</li>
      <li>Deep conditioning treatments every 1-2 weeks</li>
      <li>Minimise heat styling to prevent colour fading</li>
      <li>Protect from chlorine and sun exposure</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">The Half Head Advantage</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    Unlike full highlights, half head application allows for a more natural grow-out process. The darker underneath sections help blend regrowth, meaning you can extend time between appointments while still looking polished. This technique also preserves more of your natural hair, reducing overall chemical exposure while achieving stunning results.
  </p>

  <div class="bg-[#D3E4FD] bg-opacity-20 rounded-lg p-6">
    <p class="text-gray-700 italic">
      "Half head highlights are my go-to recommendation for clients wanting maximum impact with manageable maintenance. It's the sweet spot between transformation and natural beauty."
    </p>
  </div>
  <!-- FAQ Schema -->
  <Fragment slot="after">
    <FAQSchema 
      faqs={faqs} 
      pageUrl="https://hairbymelissa.co.nz/services/half-head-highlights/"
    />
  </Fragment>
</ServiceLayout>